{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-semantics","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Shell-specific correctness issues the generic correctness reviewer may miss: (( )) exit-code behavior under errexit, premature $- expansion in test probe strings, and Bash 3.2 compat.","prompt_body":"Examine every use of `(( _had_errexit )) && set -e` in `scripts/ship-pr.sh`: when `_had_errexit=0`, `(( 0 ))` exits with status 1 — verify this is safe under all reachable errexit states at that point and does not silently suppress errors. In `scripts/test-ship-pr.sh`, the `_run_oos_errexit_probe` function embeds `${probe}` inside a double-quoted `bash -c \"...\"` string; any `$-`, `$?`, or other special variables inside the single-quoted `probe` assignments will be expanded by the *outer* shell when the double-quoted argument is constructed — check whether this causes the assertions to verify the outer shell's `$-` instead of the inner shell's, making the tests vacuous or misleading. Also check the two `local _had_errexit=0` declarations for Bash 3.2 compatibility (`local var=val` is supported, but combined with subsequent `case $-` usage; look for any `(( ))` portability concerns on macOS system Bash 3.2). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"toggle-site-audit","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Completeness audit: are there other unconditional set -e sites in ship-pr.sh beyond the three fixed, and do functions called between save/restore have their own errexit exposure?","prompt_body":"Search `scripts/ship-pr.sh` for every `set -e` occurrence beyond the three fixed toggle sites (lines ~1126, ~1557, ~1567 in the patched file) to determine whether any unconditional `set -e` remains that could re-introduce the leak. Check whether `run_recovery_waterfall` (called between the first restore and the second save in `run_pr_prep_phase`) is itself errexit-safe when invoked with errexit active — if it internally calls subprocesses without `|| true` guards, a failure could abort `run_pr_prep_phase` before the second save/restore block executes. Verify that the early-exit path in `run_pr_prep_phase` (the `advance_phase pr-create; exit 0` block at approximately line 202 in the diff) correctly bypasses the save/restore block without leaving a dangling `set -e` state. Also check `_run_per_job_command_once` (left unchanged per the plan) — since it uses `"${_PJA_ARGV[@]}" > "$log_path" 2>&1` without `|| rc=$?`, confirm it is always called under `if`/`&&`/`||` constructs that prevent errexit from firing. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
